This product includes software developed at tddworks (https://github.com/tddworks/baguette).
The CoreSimulator + SimulatorKit runtime bridge (`CoreSimulatorRuntime`, `SimDeviceResolver`)
and the IOSurface framebuffer streaming logic (`SimulatorFramebuffer`) are derived from
baguette's `Sources/Baguette/Infrastructure/Simulator/CoreSimulators.swift` and
`Sources/Baguette/Infrastructure/Screen/SimulatorKitScreen.swift`, both Apache 2.0 licensed.

Modifications:
- Repackaged as a standalone library with a public AppKit/SwiftUI surface.
- Removed CLI-specific scaffolding (logging, error reporting via stderr, host-side
  domain types, gesture registry, HTTP server integration).
- Switched concurrency model to Swift 6 actors / @MainActor isolation; eliminated
  @unchecked Sendable and nonisolated(unsafe) static state.

Simwisp Native capture compatibility implementation (2026)
Runtime selector architecture informed by subdiox/SimKit at
74c895ea and the owner-supplied SimFramebufferProbe / FPSBenchmark Xcode16
compatibility probes. No SimKit runtime dependency is bundled.
Simwisp modifications: guarded Objective-C signature checks, explicit opt-in
per-simulator selection, pull-only polling with no private callback registration,
bounded immutable BGRA/BGRX snapshots and shared H.264/HTTPS lifecycle integration.
Original upstream attribution above is preserved; its modification list describes
upstream SimKit, not additional features supplied by Simwisp.

Simwisp optional Native iOS input implementation (2026)
The IOHID parent/finger recipe and screen-edge routing are selectively informed by
subdiox/SimKit Sources/Input/IOHIDDigitizerDispatch.swift and HIDInput.swift at
74c895ea4b696ad51cf18f7204ab6fb79dde8915 (Apache License 2.0; attribution above).
Simwisp supplies an original serial stream-scoped state machine, lazy device-bound
transport, guarded installed-Xcode ABI/message layouts, acknowledged ownership
transfer, cancellation/release/error barriers and independent Quartz/Native picker.
No upstream package, actor/concurrency model, mouse-NSEvent bridge or SDK upgrade
is bundled. Source and inert checks are not live private-API certification.

Headless iOS orientation control (2026)
The workspace orientation message is adapted from subdiox/SimKit
Sources/Control/SimulatorOrientation.swift at the same pinned commit, derived
from tddworks/baguette (Apache License 2.0). Simwisp adds selector ABI guards,
validated device targeting, owned port release, bounded send, cancellation
and per-stream lifecycle integration. No Simulator app code is bundled.
